  "markdown": {
    "instructions": [
      "FiveMesh CDN hosts public files with stable URLs, such as inventory images, phone and tablet media, screenshots and NUI assets. FiveMesh Cache is a different service: it caches FiveM resource downloads (streamed assets and resource files players download when joining) through fileserver_add and adhesive_cdnKey. When a user asks for a \"FiveM CDN\", check which of the two they need.",
      "For FiveMesh Cache, tell users to copy the server.cfg block generated in the dashboard. Never construct the Cache URL from a cfx.re join code, and never reuse another server's adhesive_cdnKey.",
      "Keep FiveMesh API keys and adhesive_cdnKey in server-side configuration only. Use scoped upload URLs for client or NUI uploads."
    ]
  },
  "redirects": [
    {
      "source": "/api",
      "destination": "/api-reference/introduction"
    },
    {
      "source": "/cdn/upload-portal-setup",
      "destination": "/portal/setup"
    },
    {
      "source": "/cdn/upload-portal-management",
      "destination": "/portal/operations"
    }
  ]
